# task-3d904491: fill the one-cell horizontal gaps

## Verified recurrence evidence
A test input was 25×7, background 0, marker color 1. Every horizontal pair (or sequence) of color-1 markers separated by exactly one 0 had that intervening cell changed to 2. All other cells stayed unchanged. The accepted output filled:
- row 2, columns 2 and 4 markers → column 3 becomes 2;
- row 4, columns 2 and 4 → column 3 becomes 2;
- row 7, columns 1 and 3 → column 2 becomes 2;
- rows 9 and 10, columns 1 and 3 → column 2 becomes 2;
- row 11, columns 0 and 2 → column 1 becomes 2;
- row 12, columns 1 and 3 → column 2 becomes 2;
- row 13, columns 0, 2, 4 → columns 1 and 3 become 2;
- row 14, columns 3 and 5 → column 4 becomes 2;
- row 15, columns 1 and 3 → column 2 becomes 2;
- row 18, columns 1 and 3 → column 2 becomes 2;
- rows 20 and 23, columns 2 and 4 → column 3 becomes 2.
Other cells, including isolated markers and vertical alignment, remained unchanged.

One demonstration used background 9 and marker 3. It changed 9 cells lying between horizontally adjacent 3s at distance two to color 2, leaving other cells unchanged. For example, row 2 had repeated `3,9,3,9,...` and all in-between 9s became 2; on other rows only the gaps bracketed by 3s were filled. This corroborates that color 2 is the inserted bridge and that only horizontally bracketed single-cell gaps are changed.

## Procedure
For each row independently, inspect every interior column `c`: if the original cells at `c-1` and `c+1` are the same non-background marker color and the middle cell is background, replace the middle cell by 2. Preserve all other cells. Do not fill vertical gaps, extend beyond endpoints, or recolor markers. If runs are consecutive, fill each qualifying gap based on the original input.

## Limits
This is direct task-ID recurrence evidence from one solved test and one demo; a fresh instance may still vary, so verify the current grid supports horizontal one-cell gaps before applying. The demo's palette differed (background 9, marker 3) but used the same replacement color 2.
